when one died according to Egyptian  mythology before they could enter the  afterlife they would have to have their  heart weighed against the feather if the  scale was balanced then they were  allowed to pass on freely if their heart  weighed heavy they were deemed unworthy  of entry their soul was devoured by a  means they would suffer a second death  with no chance of a peaceful afterlife  amat or sometimes depicted as a goddess  of the underworld but she was never  really worshipped and her image was  thought to ward off evil she was most  commonly referred to as a demon a  malevolent supernatural being her name  roughly meaning devourer of souls or  devourer of the dead  um it has the head of a crocodile the  torso of a lioness or leopard and the  lower body and hind legs of a  hippopotamus now this may sound like a  strange mixture of animals but these  were the most ferocious and terrifying  creatures known to the ancient Egyptians  the Book of the Dead referred to Emmitt  as The Punisher and executioner  and she was often believed to be the  personification of divine retribution  and justice Amit would wait in the  judgment hall of Two Truths during the  weighing of the heart ceremony those who  were deemed not fit and to the afterlife  were given one last chance to explain  their life in front of a Cyrus and his  deity judges if they were still judged  to have led a sinful life  the Nesle would be given to emit there  are variations of habits where she did  not devour the souls of the sinful at  all instead the souls who were deemed  unworthy of the afterlife were thrown  into the lake of fire  she was believed to live nearby and  acted as the guardian of the lake of  fire  although Emmet's is rarely depicted as a  goddess and more commonly seen as a  demon who devours Souls she's in no way  inherently evil she acts to ensure order  enforce good and to ward off evil she  represents that every person is given a  chance to defend their actions before  final judgment  if you've enjoyed this video then please  consider leaving a thumbs up as it helps  promote the video and allows the channel  to grow if there's anything you'd like  to discuss or have any ideas for future  videos then please let me know in the  comment section as always I've been your  host mythology and fiction explained  [Music]
 

